{
 "summary": "Converts `building-on` in `contrib/guix/toolchains.scm` from an eagerly evaluated variable into a procedure evaluated when lowering derivations. This ensures cross-toolchain packages use the target system passed via Guix's `--system` flag rather than the host system running `guix shell`.",
 "problem": "When running Guix with `--system` under emulation on a host of a different architecture (for example, `--system=aarch64-linux` on an x86_64 host), `guix shell` loads manifests before applying `--system`. As a result, `building-on` captures the host's `%current-system`, causing cross toolchains like `gcc-cross-sans-libc` to configure with mismatched `--build` triplets and fail to build.",
 "evidence": [
  "PR description demonstrates build failure: 'checking for CET support... configure: error: compiler and assembler with CET support are required for --enable-cet' when building under `--system=aarch64-linux` on x86_64",
  "PR description confirms native builds produce identical toolchain derivations to master on both `linux_static.scm` and `manifest_gui.scm`"
 ],
